      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-303366",
      ":question/problem": "A lab technician observes a population of $3, 000$ mold spores in a sample. After $6$ hours, the number of mold spores has grown to $24, 000$. Assuming exponential growth, the formula $N = A \\cdot 2^{rt}$ models the number of mold spores, where $A$ and $r$ are constants and $N$ is the number of spores $t$ hours after the initial observation. What is the value of $r$?"
    },
