      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-305162",
      ":question/problem": "In a data center, a warm heat sink was placed on a tray in a room that maintained a constant temperature of $66^{\u2218}F$. At $t = 0$ minutes, the heat sink\u2019s temperature was $194^{\u2218}F$. After $5$ minutes, its temperature had dropped to $178^{\u2218}F$, and after $10$ minutes, it was $164^{\u2218}F$. The heat sink continued to cool over time.\n\nWhich of the following functions best models the temperature $T(t)$ in degrees Fahrenheit of the heat sink $t$ minutes after it was placed on the tray?"
